[{:adr/consequences "{:no_code_changes \"by explicit user direction, this ADR ships with zero code changes --\\n                    babiniku.monetization/unprovisioned-capability is unchanged; every\\n                    subscribe/tip/PPV proposal continues to HARD-hold\", :blocked_on_etzhayyim_side \"payStream/splitDistribute/verify need to move from stub to\\n                             implementation in @etzhayyim/sdk before any of this can be built,\\n                             regardless of anything net-babiniku does\", :needs_etzhayyim_side_review \"the vendor->etzhayyim crossover pattern (decision #4) needs\\n                               review from whoever maintains ADR-2605211950/2605172100 before\\n                               net-babiniku (or any other vendor app) implements against it\", :lexicon_unimplemented \"net.babiniku.monetization.capability is a proposed lexicon,\\n                         unimplemented anywhere -- if accepted, needs a signing implementation\\n                         (client-side, inside whatever wallet-connection UI wraps\\n                         @etzhayyim/sdk's payer flow), not built by this ADR either\", :followup \"once etzhayyim's primitives exist, verify this ADR's proposed field shapes against\\n            whatever @etzhayyim/sdk actually ships -- this is a proposal, not a contract\\n            etzhayyim has agreed to\"}", :adr/authoritative_for ["net-babiniku does NOT choose its own chain/stablecoin/wallet stack -- it consumes\n    etzhayyim/root's already-decided rail (Base L2, USDC/EURC/JPYC, ERC-4337 Coinbase Smart\n    Wallet + passkey signing, Superfluid, 0xSplits, Safe) via @etzhayyim/sdk, per\n    ADR-2605211950's substrate-axis rule" "payment signing happens on the payer's own device (passkey-based Smart Wallet), NEVER on\n    net-babiniku's Cloudflare Pages Function server -- the opposite role from the LLM chat\n    call (ADR-2607070800), where the server-side secret must never reach the browser" "net.babiniku.monetization.capability (a new, payment-shaped lexicon, proposed not built)\n    is the proposed consent/authorization record shape for subscribe/tip/PPV -- distinct from\n    karute's com.etzhayyim.consent.capability, which is shaped for health-data access consent" "babiniku.monetization/unprovisioned-capability remains the only implementation for ALL\n    THREE proposal kinds (subscribe/tip/ppv) -- payStream/splitDistribute/verify in\n    @etzhayyim/sdk are unimplemented stubs today, so no entitlement can be safely unlocked yet\n    even for :tip (the one proposal kind whose settlement primitive, pay(), is real)" "the vendor-calls-etzhayyim payment-consumption crossover this ADR proposes is NEW --\n    ADR-2605211950 only worked out the opposite direction (etzhayyim calling a vendor-hosted\n    fiat XRPC) -- and needs review from etzhayyim's own ADR maintainers before being treated\n    as settled architecture"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "net-babiniku-crypto-payment-rail", :adr/related ["90-docs/adr/2607062200-net-babiniku-onlyfans-style-creator-monetization.md" "90-docs/adr/2607070800-net-babiniku-llm-backend-claude-sonnet-5.md" "orgs/etzhayyim/root/90-docs/adr/2605172100-etzhayyim-payments-on-chain-only.md" "orgs/etzhayyim/root/90-docs/adr/2605211950-vendor-centralized-etzhayyim-decentralized-substrate-axis.md" "orgs/etzhayyim/root/90-docs/adr/2605231401-karute-consent-capability-iryo-bridge.md" "orgs/etzhayyim/root/90-docs/adr/2607021800-etzhayyim-junbi-reserve-basket.md"], :adr/status "proposed", :adr/id "adr-2607071000-net-babiniku-crypto-payment-rail-etzhayyim-consumption", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-07", :adr/decision "{:no_new_chain_or_wallet {:what \"net-babiniku consumes etzhayyim's existing rail exactly as decided -- Base L2, USDC/\\n          EURC/JPYC, ERC-4337 Coinbase Smart Wallet + passkey signing, via @etzhayyim/sdk.\\n          Never imports viem, holds a key, or calls a chain RPC directly\"}, :signing_stays_client_side {:what \"the payer's Coinbase Smart Wallet is passkey-based (WebAuthn) -- the payment\\n          UserOperation must be signed in the viewer's browser, never on net-babiniku's\\n          Cloudflare Pages Function server\", :why \"matches orgs/etzhayyim/root/CLAUDE.md's substrate boundary table: 'Any platform-held\\n        private key ... in etzhayyim-operated Workers/pods/CronJobs' is Prohibited -- the same\\n        invariant applies to a vendor server proxying signing material\", :contrast_with_chat_backend \"opposite role from ADR-2607070800's LLM chat call: there, the\\n                                secret (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY) must stay server-side and never\\n                                reach the browser; here, the signing capability must stay in\\n                                the payer's browser/device and never be proxied through\\n                                net-babiniku's server. The server's only role is to receive and\\n                                verify a settlement receipt before honoring an entitlement.\"}, :new_lexicon {:what \"net.babiniku.monetization.capability -- proposed, follows karute's signed/scoped/\\n          expiring/revocable pattern but with payment-shaped fields, NOT a reuse of\\n          com.etzhayyim.consent.capability\", :shape {:amount \"{asset: \\\"USDC\\\"|\\\"EURC\\\"|\\\"JPYC\\\", value: string} -- string, not float,\\n                    matching PaymentReceipt's bigint-safe pattern\", :constraints \"{maxTotalValue?: string, revocable: bool}\", :expiresAt \"ISO-8601\", :payerDid \"DID -- viewer's did:key from their Smart Wallet\", :purpose \"\\\"subscribe\\\" | \\\"tip\\\" | \\\"ppv\\\"\", :signature \"{alg: \\\"ed25519\\\", value: base64, keyId: DID-verification-method}\", :scope \"{characterId, tier?, sceneId?} -- mirrors babiniku.monetization's existing\\n                   proposal shape\", :issuedAt \"ISO-8601\", :recurrence \"{intervalDays: int}, present only for :subscribe (drives payStream)\", :version 1, :payeeDid \"DID -- creator's (or platform's, for tips) did\"}, :mirrors_existing_proposal_shape \"1:1 with babiniku.monetization's {:kind :subscribe/:tip/\\n                                     :ppv, :character-id, ...} -- review-proposal's existing\\n                                     HARD-hold logic doesn't need to change shape when a real\\n                                     capability eventually replaces unprovisioned-capability\"}, :new_crossover_pattern_proposed_not_ratified {:what \"vendor calls @etzhayyim/sdk client-side for payer-signed settlement, then sends only\\n          the resulting {txHash, recordUri} receipt to its own server for Etzhayyim.verify()\\n          before honoring an entitlement -- no consent-capability record needs to reach\\n          net-babiniku's own Datomic-shaped storage beyond the receipt + verification result\", :status \"PROPOSED, not ratified -- ADR-2605211950 only worked out the opposite direction.\\n           This ADR's own Status field reflects that: net-babiniku is not the right place to\\n           unilaterally decide an etzhayyim-wide crossover pattern; whoever owns\\n           ADR-2605211950/2605172100 should review this before implementation\"}, :capability_stays_unprovisioned {:what \"babiniku.monetization/unprovisioned-capability remains the only implementation for\\n          ALL THREE proposal kinds -- this ADR's design does not change the HARD-hold status\\n          quo\", :why \"payStream (needed for :subscribe), splitDistribute (needed for the 80/20 split), and\\n        verify (needed to confirm ANY settlement before granting ANY entitlement) are all\\n        unimplemented stubs in @etzhayyim/sdk today. Even :tip, whose settlement primitive\\n        (pay()) is real, has no safe unlock path without verify().\", :purpose_of_this_adr \"so that when etzhayyim's own primitives mature, net-babiniku has a\\n                         concrete, reviewed integration plan to switch on rather than a\\n                         redesign-from-scratch\"}}", :db/id -1, :adr/problem "{:source \"user direction 2026-07-07: continuing the pivot to big decisions needing user\\n           input, chose 'crypto/chain + wallet selection' as the next area, then (after\\n           research surfaced that the chain stack is already decided at the etzhayyim level)\\n           chose 'ADR only' as this round's scope -- no code changes\", :prior_state {:what \"babiniku.monetization/unprovisioned-capability HARD-holds every subscribe/tip/ppv\\n          proposal (ADR-2607062200, honest-default) -- no payment rail has ever been designed\\n          or implemented for net-babiniku\"}, :research_findings {:chain_stack_already_decided {:source \"orgs/etzhayyim/root/90-docs/adr/2605172100 (status: proposed)\", :stack \"Base L2, USDC (EURC/JPYC also whitelisted per kawase-yui), ERC-4337 smart accounts\\n            via Coinbase Smart Wallet with WebAuthn passkey signing (payer's own device holds\\n            custody, no seed phrase/extension), Superfluid (streaming subs), 0xSplits (revenue\\n            splits), Gnosis Safe (escrow), an etzhayyim-operated Paymaster. Custom token\\n            explicitly rejected. Fiat processors prohibited in etzhayyim substrate. junbi\\n            (ADR-2607021800) already holds USDC/EURC/JPYC in a Base L2 Safe under Shamir-split\\n            custody keys as the reserve-treasury precedent.\", :conclusion \"there is no chain to pick for net-babiniku -- consuming this existing rail is\\n                the only option consistent with ADR-2605211950's substrate boundary\"}, :substrate_boundary {:source \"orgs/etzhayyim/root/90-docs/adr/2605211950 (status: active)\", :rule \"decentralized primitives (Ethereum/Base L2/ERC-4337/did:web/did:plc/etc.) are\\n          etzhayyim-EXCLUSIVE; centralized substrate (fiat/Datomic/operator storage/JWT) is\\n          vendor-EXCLUSIVE. net-babiniku is a vendor app (Cloudflare Pages, no chain code) --\\n          must never hold a private key or scaffold settlement logic itself\", :worked_crossover_direction \"only etzhayyim-calls-vendor (a vendor-hosted paid-tier fiat\\n                                XRPC an etzhayyim app calls as progressive enhancement) is\\n                                worked out. The OPPOSITE direction -- vendor calling into\\n                                etzhayyim for crypto settlement, which is what net-babiniku\\n                                needs -- has NO worked example yet\"}, :consent_capability_precedent {:source \"orgs/etzhayyim/root/20-actors/karute/actor-manifest.jsonld +\\n             90-docs/adr/2605231401 (karute<->iryo billing bridge)\", :shape \"com.etzhayyim.consent.capability: {version, granterDid, granteeDid, purpose, scope,\\n            resourceUris?, issuedAt, expiresAt, constraints{maxQueriesPerDay?, redactionLevel?,\\n            downstreamRedistribution?, auditWebhookDid?}, delegationPath?, revokedAt?/\\n            revokedBy?/revocationReason?, signature{alg, value, keyId}} -- Ed25519-signed,\\n            publicly verifiable delegation record\", :fit \"a useful TEMPLATE (signed/scoped/expiring/revocable delegation), not a drop-in fit --\\n         shaped for health-data ACCESS CONSENT (query scope, redaction level), not payment\\n         AUTHORIZATION. Also both karute and iryo are etzhayyim/root actors -- an intra-\\n         substrate handoff, not a worked vendor<->etzhayyim example.\", :honesty_note \"signConsentCapability -- the actual signing call -- is NOT implemented\\n                  anywhere; the ADR itself calls it 'currently a stub in the actor manifest'\"}, :sdk_implementation_state {:source \"orgs/etzhayyim/root/20-actors/etzhayyim-sdk/src/{index.ts,pay.ts}\", :real \"pay() -- a one-off EOA USDC transfer + AT record, returns\\n          PaymentReceipt{txHash, blockNumber, recordUri, ...}. THE ONLY REAL PRIMITIVE.\", :stubs \"payStream (Superfluid CFAv1.createFlow, TODO), payStreamStop, escrowOpen (Gnosis\\n           Safe 2-of-3 deploy, TODO), escrowRelease, splitDistribute (0xSplits\\n           distributeERC20, TODO), verify (5-step MST/anchor/Merkle-proof TODO, would return\\n           VerifyResult{included, anchoredAt?, merklePath?, reason?}) -- ALL THROW TODAY\", :relevance_to_net_babiniku \"subscriptions need payStream (stub); the 80/20 creator split\\n                               (ADR-2607062200) needs splitDistribute (stub); confirming ANY\\n                               payment before granting an entitlement needs verify() (stub) --\\n                               so even :tip, whose settlement primitive (pay()) is real, has\\n                               no safe path to unlock an entitlement without verify()\"}}}", :adr/alternatives "[{:option \"pick our own chain/wallet stack for net-babiniku, independent of etzhayyim\", :rejected_because \"directly violates ADR-2605211950's substrate-axis rule (decentralized\\n                      primitives are etzhayyim-exclusive); would also duplicate real\\n                      engineering (Base L2 integration, Paymaster, custody) etzhayyim has\\n                      already built\"} {:option \"proxy the payer's signing through net-babiniku's Cloudflare Function\", :rejected_because \"would require the server to hold or relay signing material for the\\n                      payer's passkey-based Smart Wallet, violating the explicit 'no\\n                      platform-held private key' prohibition in etzhayyim/root's CLAUDE.md\\n                      substrate boundary table. Signing must stay client-side.\"} {:option \"reuse com.etzhayyim.consent.capability as-is instead of a new lexicon\", :rejected_because \"its fields (query scope, redaction level, audit webhook) are shaped for\\n                      health-data access consent, not value-transfer authorization; forcing\\n                      payment semantics into that shape is a worse fit than a small new\\n                      lexicon following the same signed/scoped/expiring/revocable pattern\"} {:option \"treat pay()'s one working code path as enough to unlock :tip now\", :rejected_because \"without verify(), net-babiniku would have no way to confirm a claimed\\n                      payment actually settled on-chain before granting an entitlement -- worse\\n                      than the current honest HARD-hold, not better\"} {:option \"silently assume the vendor->etzhayyim crossover direction is already covered by\\n            ADR-2605211950's existing crossover clause\", :rejected_because \"that clause is directionally etzhayyim-calls-vendor (fiat progressive\\n                      enhancement); assuming it also covers vendor-calls-etzhayyim (crypto\\n                      settlement) would be inventing an architectural decision this ADR isn't\\n                      authorized to make unilaterally -- surfaced explicitly instead (decision\\n                      #4, consequences)\"}]", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607071000: net-babiniku crypto payment rail -- consuming etzhayyim's Base L2/\n          USDC settlement, no new chain/wallet decision"}]